normalized_answer:
For an implicit many-to-many relation, connect the existing categories directly through `categories.connect`. Do not use `categories.create` with a nested `category` object—that shape is for an explicit join model.

```ts
const brand = await prisma.brand.create({
  data: {
    name,
    slug,
    userId: user,
    image: uploadedImage.secure_url,
    categories: {
      connect: [
        { id: "ckzpl0del0014vcv2ctift2f1" },
        { id: "another-existing-category-id" },
      ],
    },
  },
  include: {
    categories: true,
  },
});
```

For one category, `connect` can contain a single object instead of an array. Each referenced `id` must already exist; otherwise Prisma throws an error.

Because the error shows a generated `BrandUncheckedCreateInput` without the `categories` relation, regenerate Prisma Client after changing the schema:

```bash
npx prisma generate
```

Then restart the application or development server and retry the query.

