normalized_answer:
`updateMany` is intended to apply the same `data` to every matching record, so it is not the right operation for assigning different order values to two groups.

First identify the two groups by their IDs, then update each one with its own value. Wrap both updates in a transaction so the swap is persisted as one atomic operation:

```ts
const [updatedA, updatedB] = await prisma.$transaction([
  prisma.todoGroup.update({
    where: { id: todoGroupAId },
    data: { order: 2 },
  }),
  prisma.todoGroup.update({
    where: { id: todoGroupBId },
    data: { order: 1 },
  }),
]);
```

Here, `todoGroupAId` is the group currently at order `1`, and `todoGroupBId` is the adjacent group currently at order `2`. If either update fails, the transaction rolls back both writes. The adjacent group must be determined by your application before constructing the updates.

