Prisma does not provide a built-in option to make a missing record return `{}` instead of `null`. Centralize the conversion in Prisma middleware; with current Prisma Client extensions, the equivalent approach is a query extension that wraps the query result.

Illustrative shape (adapt it to your Prisma version):

```ts
const prisma = new PrismaClient().$extends({
  query: {
    $allModels: {
      async $allOperations({ args, query }) {
        const result = await query(args);
        return result === null ? {} : result;
      },
    },
  },
});
```

The shown hook is broad, so restrict the conversion to the intended find/read operations if other operations should retain their normal results. This keeps the null-to-empty-object logic in one place rather than repeating `|| {}` in every NestJS handler. The code above is an illustrative shape, not a version-verified drop-in snippet.

