normalized_answer:
Yes. Prisma supports selecting specific fields from nested relations by placing a `select` inside the relation field:

```ts
const users = await prisma.user.findMany({
  select: {
    name: true,
    posts: {
      select: {
        title: true,
      },
    },
  },
})
```

The result contains each user's `name` and, under `posts`, only each post's `title`:

```json
{
  "name": "Prisma",
  "posts": [
    { "title": "PostgreSQL Database" },
    { "title": "All about databases" }
  ]
}
```

Use `select` for the scalar fields you want at each relation level. Prisma documents that selecting fields makes the result type correspond to the selected fields, so you do not need to retrieve all nested fields and remove them afterward.

