Hey @Suniron, currently you cannot alias a field returned by the prisma client without raw database access.
You can map the returned object, shaping it according to your needs, before you actually use it:
function getUser(): Omit<User, 'name'> & { alias: string } {
 return PRISMA.user.findFirst().then(
 (user) => ({ ...user, alias: name, })
 );
}
function getUsers(): Array<Omit<User, 'name'> & { alias: string }> {
 return PRISMA.user.findMany().then(
 (users) => users.map(
 ({ name, ...user }) => ({ ...user, alias: name })
 )
 );
}

