If you are using Prisma with MongoDB, define `bookmark` as a `Json` field. This allows the field to contain an object whose keys are dynamic post IDs and whose values contain the corresponding post data:

```prisma
model Books {
  id        String @id @default(auto()) @map("_id") @db.ObjectId
  bookmarks Json?
}
```

A value for `bookmarks` can then have this shape:

```json
{
  "1": {
    "id": "1",
    "title": "hello"
  },
  "2": {
    "id": "2",
    "title": "world"
  }
}
```

Because `bookmarks` is JSON, new post-ID keys can be added or removed without changing the Prisma model. Prisma's `Json` type is intended for reading, writing, and basic filtering of JSON values, including objects with dynamically named keys.

