Prisma does not support SQL-style column aliases such as `quizId: 'id'` or `quizTitle: 'title'` directly in a `select`. Select the actual Prisma fields, then rename them in JavaScript:

```ts
const quizzes = await prisma.quiz.findMany({
  select: {
    id: true,
    title: true,
  },
});

const renamed = quizzes.map((q) => ({
  quizId: q.id,
  quizTitle: q.title,
}));
```

Prisma Client extensions can add computed fields to query results, which may be useful for exposing additional names such as `quizId`. However, that is not the same as SQL `AS`: extensions add fields and do not directly rename or replace the original field in the query.

