Register `pwa` as a custom Tailwind variant with a plugin, using the same media condition you already use for standalone mode:

```js
const plugin = require('tailwindcss/plugin')

module.exports = {
  // ...
  plugins: [
    plugin(function ({ addVariant }) {
      addVariant('pwa', '@media all and (display-mode: standalone)')
    }),
  ],
}
```

Then use it on individual utilities:

```jsx
<button className="mb-2 md:mb-4 pwa:mb-6" />
```

The `pwa:` variant will apply `mb-6` only when the browser reports `display-mode: standalone`. The plugin API shown here is the relevant configuration mechanism; exact configuration details can vary with the Tailwind version. The supplied accepted example uses the same `addVariant` approach but targets `display-mode: browser`, so use `standalone` for the PWA-only behavior requested here.

The local Tailwind documentation also describes variants as the mechanism for conditionally applying styles, including stacking variants such as `hover:focus`.

