normalized_answer:
Tailwind CSS 4 requires you to make the configuration explicit or move the animation definition into CSS.

**Option 1: keep `tailwind.config.ts`**

Add an `@config` directive to the CSS file where Tailwind is imported, pointing to your configuration file. Adjust the relative path to match your project layout. This makes Tailwind load the existing `theme.extend.keyframes` and `theme.extend.animation` entries.

**Option 2: migrate the animation to the v4 CSS configuration**

Define the animation in an `@theme` block in your Tailwind CSS entry file:

```css
@theme {
  --animate-custom-pulse: custom-pulse 1s infinite ease-in-out;

  @keyframes custom-pulse {
    0%, 100% {
      transform: scale(1.32);
    }

    50% {
      transform: scale(1.1);
    }
  }
}
```

Then apply it with the `animate-custom-pulse` utility. Tailwind’s v4 animation documentation uses this same pattern: an `--animate-*` theme variable together with its `@keyframes` definition.

