Yes. In Tailwind CSS, the HTML element resets are provided by Preflight in the `base` layer. Exclude them by importing Tailwind’s theme and utilities separately, but omit `preflight.css`:

```css
@layer theme, base, components, utilities;

@import "tailwindcss/theme.css" layer(theme);
@import "tailwindcss/utilities.css" layer(utilities);
```

This keeps the utility classes while preventing Preflight’s element-style overrides, such as removing default margins, unstyling headings and lists, and constraining images.

