If the app uses Tailwind CSS v4, use the `@source` directive in the app’s Tailwind CSS stylesheet rather than relying on `tailwind.config.js` content scanning. Register the package path explicitly, relative to that stylesheet:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";
@source "../node_modules/@acmecorp/ui-lib";
```

Replace the path with the actual workspace package path. This is needed because Tailwind does not scan `node_modules` by default, and dependencies are commonly ignored during source detection.

In a monorepo, also check the scan base path. Tailwind uses the current working directory by default; if the build runs from the monorepo root, set the import’s `source(...)` base path explicitly, for example:

```css
@import "tailwindcss" source("../src");
```

Use paths relative to the stylesheet and adjust them to your repository layout. The relevant v4 procedure is the `@source` directive, which is the equivalent of the v3 `content` configuration. Also ensure the package contains complete, statically detectable class names; Tailwind cannot generate classes assembled dynamically through string interpolation.

