The issue is your global reset rule:

```css
* {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
}
```

It sets `margin` and `padding` to `0` on every element, so it removes the spacing that classes such as `p-4`, `m-4`, `mt-6`, and similar utilities are supposed to apply.

Remove that rule from `global.css`:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";
```

`@import "tailwindcss";` already includes Tailwind’s Preflight, which resets default margins and padding. Tailwind’s spacing utilities can then apply their own values normally.

If you need `box-sizing: border-box`, keep only that declaration in a separate rule, but do not globally set `margin` and `padding` to `0` after importing Tailwind.

