Tailwind CSS v4 is not designed to be used with Sass. The supported solution is to remove `lang="sass"` and let Tailwind process the component style as CSS:

```vue
<template>
  <h1>Hello world!</h1>
</template>

<style>
@reference "../../app.css";

h1 {
  @apply text-2xl font-bold text-red-500;
}
</style>
```

`@reference` makes the theme from `app.css` available to this separately processed Vue component style, which allows `@apply` to work. Alternatively, use the utilities directly in the template:

```vue
<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-red-500">Hello world!</h1>
```

So the Sass version cannot be made into the recommended Tailwind v4 workflow; use CSS for the component style or apply the utilities directly in the markup.

