normalized_answer:
Use the `inline` option on the `@theme` directive:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme inline {
  --color-accent: var(--accent-9);
}
```

Now `bg-accent` compiles to:

```css
.bg-accent {
  background-color: var(--accent-9);
}
```

This lets Radix UI Themes provide the runtime value for `--accent-9`. Without `inline`, Tailwind may generate `background-color: var(--color-accent)`, and `--color-accent` can be resolved in a scope where `--accent-9` is not available. Use the same pattern for other theme variables that reference runtime CSS variables.

