normalized_answer:
In Tailwind v4, register the private package as an additional source in the consuming app's Tailwind CSS stylesheet. This is configured with `@source`, rather than with a Vite file-scanning option.

For example, in the CSS file that imports Tailwind:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";
@source "../node_modules/@your-scope/private-npm-package";
```

Replace the package name and adjust the path so it is relative to that stylesheet. This explicitly makes Tailwind scan the package's TSX files, which are otherwise skipped because they are inside `node_modules`.

If the TSX files build class names dynamically, registering the source alone is not enough: Tailwind scans files as plain text, so the complete class names must appear in the source. Map values to complete class-name strings instead of constructing fragments such as `bg-${color}-600`.

If your issue is specifically with CSS variables rather than Tailwind class names, the supplied evidence does not establish the required configuration for that case.

