normalized_answer:
Tailwind CSS v4.1.4 automatically scans files throughout the project, which is why it detects classes in `public/about.html`. Disable automatic source detection and explicitly register only your authorized source directory.

In `src/style.css`, add `source(none)` to the Tailwind utilities import:

```css
@layer theme, base, components, utilities;
@import "tailwindcss/theme.css" layer(theme);
@import "tailwindcss/utilities.css" layer(utilities) source(none);
@source "../src";
```

With automatic detection disabled, Tailwind uses the explicitly registered `../src` source instead of scanning the rest of the project, so classes found only in `public/about.html` will not be included. The `@source` path is relative to the stylesheet; if `src/style.css` is the stylesheet and the intended source directory is that same `src` directory, `@source "./"` is an equivalent simplification.

