`height: auto` comes from Tailwind’s Preflight. Import Tailwind’s theme and utilities separately, but omit the Preflight import:

```css
@layer theme, base, components, utilities;

@import "tailwindcss/theme.css" layer(theme);
@import "tailwindcss/utilities.css" layer(utilities);
```

Do not use `@import "tailwindcss/preflight.css" layer(base);`. This keeps Tailwind’s theme and utilities while preventing Preflight from adding the global `img, video { height: auto; }` rule.

If you need most Preflight styles, the other supported approaches are to use your own modified copy of Preflight with that declaration removed, or run a post-processing step that removes the rule after Tailwind generates the CSS.

