The consuming application is generating less CSS because Tailwind does not automatically scan files inside `node_modules`. Since the UI kit is installed there, Tailwind does not see the Svelte component files containing the kit’s utility classes, so those utilities are omitted from the project’s output.

Explicitly register the UI kit’s compiled source files in the kit stylesheet, using a path relative to that stylesheet:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";
@source "../dist";
```

Here, `../dist` should point to the built UI-kit files that contain the component class names. Then rebuild or republish the kit and regenerate the consuming application’s CSS. The difference between the 1067-line kit output and the 436-line application output is therefore consistent with the kit’s sources being scanned internally but ignored when the kit is consumed from `node_modules`.

