Yes. Tailwind CSS v4 supports scanning source files outside the docs package, but the v3-style `content` array in `tailwind.config.ts` is not what the v4 CSS-first setup uses. In v4, JavaScript configuration is not used unless explicitly enabled for backward compatibility, and even then its `content` configuration is not used for source detection.

Register the UI source from the stylesheet that imports Tailwind:

```css
/* docs/src/index.css */
@import "tailwindcss";
@source "../../ui";
```

Because `@source` is resolved relative to `docs/src/index.css`, `../../ui` points to the sibling `packages/ui` directory in the structure shown. You can then keep the UI package as a raw source package without adding a Tailwind plugin or building a separate UI stylesheet. The docs package's Tailwind instance will scan the registered UI files and generate utilities such as `bg-blue-500`, `text-white`, `px-5`, and `py-2.5` for the docs bundle.

The relevant v4 configuration is therefore the `@source` rule in `docs/src/index.css`; the `content` entry in `docs/tailwind.config.ts` should not be relied on to solve this case.

