normalized_answer:
Tailwind 3 cannot generate a complete “full” CSS build: it is JIT-only and generates CSS only for classes it detects in your source. There is no flag or configuration option to make it emit every class.

For local testing, explicitly safelist the classes you need. In the documented syntax, add an `@source inline()` directive to your CSS, for example:

```css
@source inline("{hover:,focus:,}underline");
```

This generates `underline` plus its `hover:` and `focus:` variants. Apply the same approach to other utilities or patterns you want available during development, but generating the entire framework is not supported.

