This is most likely a content-path configuration issue, not a Tailwind bug. The generated `.bg-[url('....')]` rules look like classes from Tailwind’s own test suite, which indicates that your Tailwind `content` configuration is scanning `node_modules`.

Restrict `content` to your application source files—for example, your `src` directory and the relevant HTML/JS/JSX/TS/TSX files—and remove any broad glob that includes `node_modules`. Then delete the generated CSS and rebuild. Tailwind scans source files as plain text and generates CSS for tokens that look like utility classes, so scanning dependency files can cause these test-only URL values to be emitted. The exact configuration change depends on your current `tailwind.config.js`, which was not included.

