normalized_answer:
The border is caused by Tailwind Preflight interacting with Angular Material’s MDC outline. The affected element is `.mdc-notched-outline__notch`. Angular Material increases the focused outline parts to `border-width: 2px`, while Tailwind Preflight globally sets every element’s border style to `solid`; the resulting nonzero width becomes visible on the notch.

A targeted fix is to override the offending element’s border style in your application CSS, for example:

```css
.mdc-notched-outline__notch {
  border-style: none;
}
```

Alternatively, disable Tailwind’s Preflight/base reset in the Tailwind configuration if you do not need it. Tailwind’s documented approach is to omit the Preflight import; for the Tailwind 3 setup shown in the question, this corresponds to disabling the `preflight` core plugin. A targeted override is generally the narrower fix when keeping the rest of Preflight is important.

